📝 ABOUT THIS CLIP
Recorded live at the AI Engineer World's Fair 2026, Swyx (Shawn Wang) gives Alex Volkov of ThursdAI a candid look at how the AI Engineer World's Fair became one of the top industry events for AI engineers. He breaks down scaling from 3,000 to 7,200+ attendees, the stress-inducing Gini coefficient of last-minute ticket sales, and the origin story that runs from a Dev.to blog post to the Latent Space podcast to the influential Rise of the AI Engineer essay. Swyx also unpacks the Token Billionaire club for engineers spending $5K-$20K a month on API tokens, the JSConf-inspired plan to go international across Singapore, London, Tokyo, and beyond, and the conference culture — daily printed newspaper, puppy corner, robots, and the high-value hallway track. It's a look at why human connection matters more in an agent-driven world. Swyx is co-founder and CEO of AI Engineer and co-host of the Latent Space podcast.

